  "caption": "Niece Pip, 11, wanted to lift weights, and Uncle Quinn had heard it stunts growth. Pip's other plan was to copy an adult influencer's max-lift routine. Hmm.\n\nSupervised, well-progressed strength training is generally safe and can build strength and confidence in kids. The growth fear came largely from unsupervised maximal lifting, and it won't make kids bulky.\n\nWhat can help: technique before load, qualified supervision, no max testing for young kids, scaling down in growth spurts, and counting sport, training and rest as one total load. Basics often suit around ages 7–10, then build through the teens.\n\nIf your child has a medical condition or an injury, check in first so the plan suits them.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
